--- doc/configurable.n
+++ doc/configurable.n
@@ -144,11 +144,15 @@
 .SH "ADVANCED USAGE"
 .PP
 The configurable class system is comprised of several pieces. The
 \fBoo::configurable\fR metaclass works by mixing in a class and setting
 definition namespaces during object creation that provide the other bits and
-pieces of machinery. The key pieces of the implementation are enumerated here
+pieces of machinery. Because of this, a configurable class that also needs
+other mixins must add them with \fBmixin \-append\fR; a plain \fBmixin\fR
+replaces the whole mixin list, including \fBoo::configuresupport::configurable\fR,
+and the \fBconfigure\fR method disappears.
+The key pieces of the implementation are enumerated here
 so that they can be used by other code:
 .\" COMMAND: configurable
 .TP
 \fBoo::configuresupport::configurable\fR
 .

